--!nonstrict
--[[
	restaurant_bind.luau (TASK-382, MAP-01 r4 "Corner Dogs"; DEC-269..DEC-280; levels/MAP-01-r4-restaurant.md rev. 2;
	tech/restaurant-flow.md §4.1). Edit-mode Studio snippet, NOT gameplay code. NO Place.run / Bind.run.

	run("assetplace/restaurant_bind", mode)
	  "dry"       report only (lot, what exists, what would move), writes nothing
	  "blockout"  shell, counters, named binding Parts and points in flat blockout colours (step 2 of the task)
	  nil/"apply" blockout + art pass (step 3): materials, tile textures, pack meshes from ServerStorage.__AssetCache
	  "undo"      restaurant -> ServerStorage.TrailerBackup.Restaurant_Undone (tags off), trailer and everything moved
	              back (poses from _RST_Orig* attributes, backed-up items to their recorded parent), tags restored

	Idempotent: running "apply" twice gives the same place. Everything it builds lives in workspace.MAP01_Restaurant (a
	Folder, outside MAP01_Assets so a Place.run does not wipe it); the vehicle Model is MAP01_Restaurant.TRL
	(tag Vehicle, Vehicle = "trailer", ModelStreamingMode Persistent). Parts it builds are found by name and rewritten.
	Nothing is destroyed: trailer-only things are MOVED to ServerStorage.TrailerBackup (attribute OrigPath, OrigTags; the
	gameplay tags are removed in the backup so no service scans a ghost); things that are reused (tables, sign, crates,
	bins, CCTV, menu board, points, nodes, light zones) keep their first pose in _RST_OrigCF / _RST_OrigLinks / _RST_OrigSize.

	Kitchen: the trailer's stations and anchors are CLONED (with their tags) into TRL and placed on the new counters, so the
	boot keeps the exactly-one-per-kind rule of MapIndex/Required (Restaurant.Rules.Enabled = false) and the restaurant one
	(Enabled = true: coffee + phone + switch + shutter, Tablet / Pickup tags, PU-1..8). Clones keep their legacy names and
	MapId (TRL-PHONE, TRL-TIPJAR, TRL-BREAKER are read by code); the r4 id is the attribute RestaurantId. Second copies of a
	kind (CUT-2) are blockout Models WITHOUT the Station tag (attribute PendingStation = kind) until the coders enable them.
	All numbers are MAP-01 coordinates (+X east, +Z south); world = (-x, y, K - z) (map_frame.luau).
]]

